# Codebase Archaeologist — environment template.
#
# Variable names and defaults come from internal/envx/envx.go. Copy to .env
# (or .env.local) in the working directory; a .env file is loaded into the
# process environment at startup (existing real env vars always win).
# No value here is a secret in code — credentials come from the environment.

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Primary driver switch. When set, the store opens Postgres with this DSN.
# Leave unset for local SQLite development (default).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://archaeologist:archaeologist@localhost:5432/archaeologist
#
# Fallback DSN, read only when DATABASE_URL is empty.
# ARCH_POSTGRES_DSN=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db
#
# Set to "true" to force the SQLite driver even when a DSN is present
# (local-only mode for sensitive codebases).
# ARCH_LOCAL_ONLY=

# --- Service (the Chi API under service/) -----------------------------------
# Listen address for the API service. CLI-only usage can leave this default.
ARCH_BIND=:8080
#
# API key. Empty disables authentication (CLI-only / local single-user mode);
# when set, every service request must carry it in the Authorization header.
# ARCH_AUTH_KEY=

# --- Paths and tooling ------------------------------------------------------
# Where the SQLite database file and git working snapshots live.
ARCH_DATA_DIR=./data
#
# Path to the Rust tree-sitter parser binary. Empty means the
# "archaeologist-parser" binary on $PATH (the image ships it there).
# ARCH_PARSER_BIN=archaeologist-parser
#
# Log level: debug | info | warn | error
ARCH_LOG_LEVEL=info
